throughout the Second World War in  Europe there were many neutral nations  who despite their government's  intentions were unable to stay so while  some like Finland were able to resist  others like Sweden managed to avoid  fighting given Sweden's immense natural  resources notably iron it's even more  surprising that it was left alone when  the powers around it were fighting for  their continued existence not only that  but Sweden would have been a valuable  ally to whichever side it joined which  raises the question why didn't Sweden  join World War two and how did it manage  to maintain its neutrality and deter  aggressors so when the war broke out  Sweden declared itself to be a non  belligerent this shouldn't be surprising  since Sweden had been a neutral nation  since after the Napoleonic Wars this was  mostly because it was forced to hand  over Swedish Pomerania to Prussia and  thus had nothing binding them to  mainland continental politics  thus by 1939 Sweden had over a century  of neutral foreign policy stances behind  it it was governed at this point by per  Albin Hansson who was doing everything  in his power to keep fascist or  communist sympathizers away from power  his government was a coalition of four  major parties and their foreign policy  goals at first was simply don't get  involved in the war yet as many of you  will be aware the war soon came to its  neighbors Finland fought the winter war  against the USSR and in 1940 both  Denmark and Norway were conquered by  Germany for the Finnish Soviet Wars the  Swedish were sympathetic to Finland and  there were even some who called for  Sweden to formally get involved hansom  resisted and so Sweden covertly gave  money and weapons to the Finns and  roughly 12,000 Swedes crossed the border  to help in non-combat roles as for  Denmark and Norway Sweden wasn't willing  to go to such lengths to help them  resist Germany and this was largely for  economic reasons  Sweden exported masses of iron ore to  Germany throughout the war and given  that everyone else had been conquered  there was no other customers in case  you're wondering the reason why Germany  kept buying the iron instead of simply  conquering Sweden was a Hitler assumed  that the Allies wouldn't bomb a neutral  country so the only reason that Sweden  was able to stay neutral was that it  made concessions to both sides for  example when Germany conquered Norway  the Swedish government allowed German  troops to travel through the country  they also allowed German troops to  transit the country to Finland in 1941  when Germany invaded the Soviet Union  this actually led to what's called the  midsummer crisis where ministers  panicked over what to do because they  really didn't want to be seen aiding the  Germans in the war with the USSR in fact  Sweden's King Gustaf v said that if the  Germans weren't accommodated then he  personally would not be willing to bear  the consequences and so they allowed  German troops to cross and throughout  the war over  two million German soldiers did so of  course Sweden couldn't just give in to  what the Germans wanted since at that  point they may as well have just been a  member of the axis and as such Sweden  was sure to aid the Allies too for  example it took thousands of Jewish  refugees from Denmark and all over  Europe as well as giving refuge to  socialists and political dissidents and  furthermore Sweden also took to covertly  training Norwegian troops in its  territory they were also active in  conducting espionage against Germany and  fed troop movements and industrial  information to the British in the  Americans and in the end Sweden's  neutrality in the war carries a  confusing legacy avoiding occupation and  bombing was the priority for the  government and they did achieve that  they did so by facilitating German troop  movements and providing it with valuable  resources with which it could power its  war machine that said what real choice  did Sweden have Denmark or Norway were  conquered for reasons of strategy and  the Germans would have happily done the  same to Sweden and Sweden was sure to  balance this were evading the Allies and  giving refuge to Europe's persecuted in  the end Sweden state neutral by doing  just enough to avoid the ire of both  sides I hope you enjoyed this episode  and thank you for watching with extra  thanks to my patreon supporters which  you can see on screen and with an extra  special thanks to James Bissonnette  David archaeologist Ozark a flash Party  Boyko Rob Waterhouse Chris wicker  Michael Reynolds Gustav Swann David  Silverman spinning three plates  Maggie packs Kowski Christian check'  Anthony Beckett Ike Skye Chappell and  Winston K wood  you
 

